 "notes": {
  "blend-fill": "A blend mode per fill: the engine mixes each paint in its own layer, the DOM renderer with background-blend-mode (which only blends with the paints of the same box, so the two may differ where the box is translucent).",
  "fill-modes": "Crop, Tile and Rotate 90 in the engine and the DOM renderer; corner smoothing is engine-only (the DOM draws a circular corner).",
  "mask": "Use as mask: the ellipse cuts the layers above it; the grey under it shows outside.",
  "mask-path": "A slanted path as mask, its viewBox scaled to the layer: the layers above are cut to the outline, not its box.",
  "image-fit": "The format has no tile mode (cover, contain, stretch only), so tiling has no fixture.",
  "text-letter-spacing": "Auto tracking is stored as a plain letterSpacing number; the values here come from src/tracking.ts autoTracking().",
  "text-wrap": "The format has no truncation or ellipsis property; a fixed-width-height box overflows in both renderers.",
  "layout-extras": "Canvas-only auto layout (wrap, min/max, evenly, baseline, first on top, negative gap, included stroke, hug with a fill child): html.ts draws without these, so fidelity is a known gap and the regression baseline is the check.",
  "tile-seams": "Hairlines and text differ from Chrome everywhere at these zooms (see findings), so this fixture is judged on the seam check: mismatches within 2 px of a tile edge against the rest of the view."
 }
}
